.TH FERRENT-CLI 1 "2026-11-22" "ferrent-cli 0.1.2" "Ferrent"
.SH NAME
ferrent-cli \- control a Ferrent daemon over TLS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ferrent-cli
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ferrent-cli
talks to the Ferrent daemon's TLS gRPC API. It lists and edits torrents,
manages labels and trackers, and imports Deluge state.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-server \fIURL\fR
daemon address (default \fIhttps://localhost:50051\fR)
.TP
.B \-\-ca \fIFILE\fR
CA certificate used to pin the daemon
.TP
.B \-\-token \fITOKEN\fR
API token; the daemon generates it on first install
.TP
.B \-\-json
machine-readable output where the command supports it
.SH COMMANDS
.BR add ,
.BR list ,
.BR show ,
.BR pause ,
.BR resume ,
.BR remove ,
.BR files ,
.BR trackers ,
.BR web-seeds ,
.BR blocklist ,
.BR create ,
.BR recheck ,
.BR rename-file ,
.BR move ,
.BR disks ,
.BR config ,
.BR rss ,
.BR import-deluge ,
.BR watch ,
.BR set ,
.BR notify .
Run
.B ferrent-cli \fICOMMAND\fB \-\-help\fR
for the flags of one command.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ferrent/token
token generated by the package's postinst
.TP
.I /var/lib/ferrent/tls-cert.pem
CA certificate the daemon creates on first start
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ferrentd (1),
.BR ferrent-gui (1)
